      "favorited" : false,
      "full_text" : "@DwightEichorn I’d say the conservative estimate on the duration for the 104° rotation is 24 hours. Along the 31st meridian this translates to a velocity of &gt;400 km/h on the surface. If we assume 6 hours, this rises to over 1,800 Km/h. Flash freeze conditions; such as in Alaska/Siberia ‘muck’.",
      "lang" : "en",
