      "full_text" : "@not2btrifldwith @HamEggsnSam @EthicalSkeptic @MJAsmo The Dzhanibekov effect is reliably cyclic and predictable. Barring friction or other perturbing force, a spinning object in a weightless environment will regularly undergo alternating rotations indefinitely. There is nothing to suggest the earth is not subject to this.",
