      "possibly_sensitive" : false,
      "created_at" : "Sun Jun 16 14:54:06 +0000 2024",
      "favorited" : false,
      "full_text" : "The estimated magnetic field near the Earth's core is 25-40 teslas. The CERN|LHC contains 1,232 superconducting dipole electromagnets, each capable of 8.3 teslas (20-33% of that near the core), for a theoretical combined total of 10,225 teslas (if energized simultaneously). https://t.co/M4lhEvYReL",
