      "full_text" : "@captainripsaw I'm tinkering with the idea that certain periods when the gas giants' net gravitational influence is close to zero may be when bodies which are normally axially stabilized by tidal locking (ie. Earth-Sun) may become gravitationally disrupted, precipitating a Dhanibekov rotation.",
