      "full_text" : "@emigenix @SeverinAlexB Erratics, by definition are 'out of place'. They have been transported by agencies other than gravity (normally water or ice) to locations far from their parent stone, often hundreds of kilometers from the source. The Jura erratics are over 50km to the north of the Alps.",
